! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1262 ("TEST EX AND EXIC"), TEST 2A --
! "CHECK THAT EXIC WILL NOT RELINQUISH CONTROL, AND THE TWO POSSIBLE
! MEMORY COMBINATIONS".  Entry I6247 at 023576.40, last row 023704.40.
! PDF pp.96, 97, 98 of docs/jb_ax5b_ibox-5.pdf, transcribed WHOLE.
!
! CITED BY PDF PAGE.  jb_ax5b's LISTING pages carry no printed page
! numbers -- the "12 11 10 9" down the left margin is fanfold
! carriage-tape line numbering, and the only printed numbers are in the
! front write-up, which is scanned 2-up.  Every verify_ax5b_*.py here
! already says "PDF p.NN" for that reason.
!
! EXTENT, ESTABLISHED FIRST-HAND AT 500 dpi AND NOT FROM THE BLOCK MAP.
! PDF p.95's last three rows are 023575.00 "LX,$X13,IC262" /
! 023575.40 "V+,$X13,BIT3" / 023576.00 "SX,$X13,IC262" -- TEST 1D's
! continuity bridge.  The very next printed row, the first on PDF p.96,
! is 023576.40 with I6247 in the name field.  PDF p.98's last printed
! row is 023704.40 "SX,$X13,IC262"; everything below it on that page is
! blank fanfold rule.  So the block is exactly pp.96-98 and exactly
! 023576.40-023704.40.
!
! CLOSURE ARITHMETIC.  023576.40 through 023704.40 inclusive is
! (0o23704 - 0o23576) * 2 + 1 = 70 * 2 + 1 = 141 half-words.  FOUR rows
! are full-word VFL loads (023630.00, 023641.40, 023663.40, 023675.00),
! each one printed row occupying two half-words, so the page prints
! 141 - 4 = 137 rows.  This file has 137 ROWS entries and no SLC but the
! first.  Nothing is left behind and nothing is doubled.
!
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT "MUST NOT RELINQUISH CONTROL" ACTUALLY MEANS
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! The block map's phrase is second-hand.  Read off these three pages,
! the deck's own claim is narrower and sharper: AFTER AN "EXIC" THE
! INSTRUCTION COUNTER MUST GO ON IN THE MAIN PROGRAM, AT THE HALF-WORD
! FOLLOWING THE "EXIC" ITSELF.  Control must not be handed to any of
! the three OTHER places the EXIC touched.  The deck does not argue
! this -- it PLANTS A TRAP AT EACH OF THE THREE and checks none fired.
!
!   (1) NOT to the half-word after the pseudo-instruction counter.
!       "SVA,$X1,I62BR1" writes the error label into the "$BD,0" that
!       PDF p.109 prints at 024323.40 -- the RIGHT half of the very
!       word 024323.00 that holds the pseudo-IC.  If the machine ran on
!       from the pseudo-IC word, that BD fires.
!         023610.00  I6249  "-EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT"
!         023610.40         "-FOLLOWING PSEUDO IC."
!
!   (2) NOT to the half-word after the SUBJECT instruction.
!       "SVA,$X1,I62BR2" writes the error label into the "$BD,0" at
!       024325.00.  THE ARITHMETIC, SHOWN rather than asserted: the
!       subject slot I62SUB is 024324.00; the subject planted in it is
!       I62EXV, which PDF p.109 prints as "L(BU),I00O" with the
!       TWO-WORD machine code "24503.00 80 000000.20 50", i.e. FULL
!       LENGTH; a full-length instruction at 024324.00 occupies
!       024324.00 AND 024324.40; so the next instruction location is
!       024324.40 + 32 bits = 024325.00, which is exactly where p.109
!       prints I62BR2.  Had the subject been half-length the trap
!       would have had to sit at 024324.40 instead.  If the machine ran
!       on from the subject, that BD fires.
!         023611.40  I6250  "-EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT"
!         023612.00         "-FOLLOWING INSTRUCT ADDRESSED BY PSIC."
!
!   (3) NOT INTO the pseudo-IC word itself.  This one has no planted
!       trap because it needs none: PDF p.109 prints I62PSI at
!       024323.00 as "LX,$X0,0", a REAL INSTRUCTION whose address field
!       the SVA then fills in.  Used as the manual says -- as data --
!       it is a pseudo-instruction counter; EXECUTED, it would load
!       word I62SUB into $X0.  So the deck zeroes $X0 before the EXIC
!       and reads it back after:
!         023614.40  Z,$X0
!         023641.40  L(BU),$X0
!         023643.00  BZRZ,SERS   "-INST AT PSIC WAS EXECUTED."
!       THREE control-flow violations, not two.  This is the one the
!       block map's phrase does not hint at.
!
! And the fourth thing "control" means here, checked first of all:
!   (0) NOT to the interruption address.  "SVA,$X1,I62ITE" plants the
!       error label in the interrupt-table entry, $IND and $MASK are
!       zeroed, and an interruption would land on
!         023606.40  I6248  "-INT ON EXIC TO PSIC IN MAIN TO"
!         023607.00         "-VFL LOAD IN MAIN."
!
! THE PRIMARY SOURCE SAYS EXACTLY THIS, and it is the sentence the
! block map is compressing.  Reference Manual 22-6530-2, PRINTED p.49
! (PDF p.52; PDF page = printed page + 3), read first-hand at 400 dpi
! for this file:
!
!   "In either of the execution instructions, the subject instruction
!   may be of any type and is performed according to the normal rules
!   for an operation of its type.  HOWEVER, IN ORDER THAT THE MAIN
!   PROGRAM MAY HAVE FULL CONTROL AT ALL TIMES, THE SUBJECT
!   INSTRUCTION IS NOT ALLOWED TO CHANGE THE STATE OF THE INTERRUPTION
!   SYSTEM OR REPLACE THE CONTENTS OF THE INSTRUCTION COUNTER."
!
! Same printed page, on the pseudo-IC and on the counter:
!
!   "...EXECUTE INDIRECT AND COUNT, specifies a location which imitates
!   the instruction counter, a pseudo-instruction counter.  The
!   pseudo-instruction counter addresses the location of a single
!   subject instruction, which is fetched and executed.  After the
!   subject instruction has been fetched, but prior to its execution,
!   the pseudo-instruction counter is stepped."
!
!   "When an execution operation is initiated in the main program, the
!   instruction counter is stepped in normal fashion as in all
!   operations of the main program.  However, it is never stepped
!   during the execution of any subject instruction even if the subject
!   instruction is again one of the execution instructions."
!
! Reference Manual PRINTED p.50 (PDF p.53), read first-hand at 400 dpi:
!
!   "Execute Indirect and Count (EXIC).  Bits 0-18 of the full-word
!   addressed by BITS 0-17 of the effective address are used as a
!   pseudo-instruction counter."
!
!   "Any actuated indicator whose mask bit is on may cause interruption
!   at the completion, termination, or suppression of an execution
!   operation."
!
! C22-6531 "STRAP-1", APPENDIX A, PRINTED p.56 (PDF p.57), read
! first-hand at 400 dpi.  Every system symbol this block names is in
! its "Word No. / Bit Address" columns, so no register address here is
! taken from the assembler's own table on trust:
!   $ IA 1 Interruption Address 2 0-17   | $ IND 1 Indicators 11 0-63
!   $ MASK 1 Mask 12 21-49               | $ L 1 Left Half of Acc 8 0-63
!   $ R 1 Right Half of Acc 9 0-63       | $ X0 1 Index Zero 16 0-63
!   $ X2 1 Index Two 18 0-63             | $ X13 1 Index Thirteen 29
!   $ X14 1 Index Fourteen 30 0-63       | $ X15 1 Index Fifteen 31
!   $ RZ 2 Result Zero 11 57             | $ XE 2 Index Equal 11 53
! Decimal 2, 11, 12, 8, 9, 16, 18, 30, 31 are octal 2, 13, 14, 10, 11,
! 20, 22, 36, 37 -- exactly the address fields this block prints.
!
! Reference Manual PRINTED p.23 (PDF p.26), read first-hand at 400 dpi,
! for the index-word fields the verification body walks and for the
! 18-bit exception:
!
!   "In the majority of these operations, 19 bits of the effective
!   address are used in order to permit addressing of half-words.  THE
!   TWO EXCEPTIONS USE ONLY 18 BITS OF THE EFFECTIVE ADDRESS BECAUSE
!   THEY REQUIRE FULL-WORD OPERANDS."
!
!   "Index Equal (XE).  This indicator is set to one when the field in
!   the index specified by J is equal to the comparand.  It is set to
!   zero when the index field is lower or higher than the comparand."
!
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! THE BLOCK'S STRUCTURE, AND THE "TWO MEMORY COMBINATIONS"
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! TEST 1A is described as "EX must not relinquish control; SEVEN memory
! combinations".  TEST 2A announces its own analogue in its header, in
! so many words:
!
!   023576.40  I6247  LVI,$X1,I62INT  "-TEST 2A, CHECK THAT EXIC WILL NOT"
!   023577.00         SVA,$X1,$IA     "-RELINQUISH CONTROL,AND THE TWO"
!   023577.40         LVI,$X1,I6248   "-POSSIBLE MEMORY COMBINATIONS."
!
! TWO, not seven, and the deck names them itself:
!
!   023612.40  "-TEST MEMORY COMBOS."  "-EXIC IN MAIN."
!   023613.40                          "-PSIC IN MAIN."   "-SUBJ IN MAIN."
!   023645.40                          "-EXIC IN MAIN."
!   023646.00                          "-PSIC IN IX STG." "-SUBJ IN MAIN."
!
! ONLY THE PSEUDO-IC MOVES.  The EXIC is in the main program both times
! (it is the instruction being tested), and the subject is in main
! storage both times (p.50: subject instructions of EXIC "may occupy any
! available locations with addresses 32.00 and greater", which rules
! index storage out).  The pseudo-IC is the one participant that can sit
! in either, so there are exactly two combinations.  The second is made
! by "LX,$X2,I62PSI" at 023654.00 -- copy the pseudo-IC word into index
! register 2 -- and then "EXIC,$X2" at 023656.40 instead of
! "EXIC,I62PSI".  THAT IS THE WHOLE DIFFERENCE IN THE INSTRUCTION.
!
! SO THE BLOCK IS THREE PASSES, NOT THREE TESTS:
!
!   PASS 0   023576.40-023612.00   the bare relinquish test.  PSIC in
!            main.  Plants the interrupt entry and both traps, runs
!            one EXIC, and checks NOTHING ELSE -- it never zeroes $X0,
!            $R, $L, $IND or $MASK, so it CANNOT check execution or
!            stepping.  Three error entries (I6248/I6249/I6250) and no
!            verification body at all.
!   PASS 1   023612.40-023645.00   "-TEST MEMORY COMBOS." -- the SAME
!            memory configuration as pass 0, re-run with the full
!            verification body.  Error entries I6252/I6253/I6254, body
!            at I6255.
!   PASS 2   023645.40-023704.40   PSIC in index storage.  Error
!            entries I6256/I6257/I6258, body at I6259, then routine
!            1262's TEST 2A exit and continuity bridge.
!
! PASSES 1 AND 2 ARE THE SAME SHAPE, ROW FOR ROW, and saying so plainly
! is a deliverable in itself: after the first two the block does not
! introduce a new idea, it re-runs one.  The differences are seven, all
! small, and all of them transcribed rather than normalised:
!   a. the pseudo-IC operand: "EXIC,I62PSI" vs "EXIC,$X2";
!   b. pass 2 carries the extra "LX,$X2,I62PSI" (023654.00);
!   c. the stepping check reads "LX,$X1,I62PSI" (023643.40) in pass 1
!      and "LX,$X1,$X2" (023677.00) in pass 2 -- same question, asked
!      of whichever copy the EXIC was told to use;
!   d. the clear-indicators call is "BD,I60S1" (023620.40) in pass 1
!      and "B,I60S1" (023653.40) in pass 2;
!   e. the SC pair and the SR pair are in OPPOSITE ORDER (below);
!   f. pass 1 has the "-TEST MEMORY COMBOS." heading line, pass 2 has
!      no heading and its three class comments sit one row higher;
!   g. pass 1's error text says "ON MAIN" where every sibling says
!      "IN MAIN" -- a DECK TYPO, measured below.
!
! THE VERIFICATION BODY (I6255, I6259), SIX CHECKS IN ORDER:
!   1. "L(BU),$R / SIC,SEN / BRZ,SERS"    "-EXIC SUBJ INST NOT EXECUTED."
!      $R was zeroed; the subject "L(BU),I00O" must have made it
!      nonzero.  BRZ -- error when Result Zero is ON.
!   2. "LX,$X14,I62EXV / LX,$X15,I62SUB / KV / BZXE,SERS"
!                                         "-BITS 0-24 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD."
!   3. "SC,$Xn,$Xn / SC,$Xm,$Xm / KV / BZXE"
!                                         "-BITS 28-45 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD."
!   4. "SR,$Xn,$Xn / SR,$Xm,$Xm / KV / BZXE"
!                                         "-BITS 46-63 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD."
!   5. "L(BU),$X0 / SIC,SEN / BZRZ,SERS"  "-INST AT PSIC WAS EXECUTED."
!   6. "LX,$X1,<psic> / KVI,$X1,I62SUB / BXE,SERS"
!                                         "-PSEUDO IC UNCHANGED BY EXIC."
!
! CHECKS 2-4 ARE ONE IDEA IN THREE ROWS: the master subject I62EXV and
! the working copy in I62SUB are both loaded AS INDEX WORDS, and the
! three comparisons walk the three index fields -- VALUE 0-24, COUNT
! 28-45, REFILL 46-63 (Reference Manual printed p.23's index-word
! layout; bits 25-27 are unused, which is why the deck's three messages
! cover 0-24, 28-45 and 46-63 and nothing in between).  "KV" compares
! only the value field, so "SC,$X15,$X15" -- store index 15's COUNT into
! the word at location $X15, which IS index 15 -- moves the count field
! into the value field so that the same KV can see it.  Same trick with
! SR for the refill.  THE DECK COMPARES A 64-BIT INSTRUCTION WORD WITH
! AN INSTRUCTION THAT ONLY COMPARES 25 BITS, THREE TIMES.
!
! THE ONE THING TEST 2A CHECKS THAT ITS TWIN 2B DOES NOT, AND THE ONE
! IT CHECKS MORE WEAKLY -- this is what the EXIC implementation wants:
!   * 2A checks that the pseudo-IC word was NOT EXECUTED (check 5).
!     TEST 2B has no such row anywhere.
!   * 2A's stepping check (check 6) is STRICTLY WEAKER THAN 2B's and
!     the opposite polarity.  2B does "V+I,$X2,0.32 / KV,$X2,I62PSI /
!     BZXE" -- the pseudo-IC must have stepped by EXACTLY the subject's
!     length.  2A does "KVI,$X1,I62SUB / BXE" -- error when the
!     pseudo-IC is still EQUAL to where it started.  2A only demands
!     that it CHANGED.  Do not read 2B's contract out of 2A's rows.
!
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY ERROR MESSAGE AND HEADING IN THE RANGE, VERBATIM, IN ADDRESS
! ORDER, WITH ITS OCTAL LOCATION
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
!   023576.40  "-TEST 2A, CHECK THAT EXIC WILL NOT"
!   023577.00  "-RELINQUISH CONTROL,AND THE TWO"
!   023577.40  "-POSSIBLE MEMORY COMBINATIONS."
!   023606.00  "-PSIC IS PSEUDO IC."
!   023606.40  "-INT ON EXIC TO PSIC IN MAIN TO"
!   023607.00  "-VFL LOAD IN MAIN."
!   023610.00  "-EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT"
!   023610.40  "-FOLLOWING PSEUDO IC."
!   023611.40  "-EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT"
!   023612.00  "-FOLLOWING INSTRUCT ADDRESSED BY PSIC."
!   023612.40  "-TEST MEMORY COMBOS."
!   023613.00  "-EXIC IN MAIN."
!   023613.40  "-PSIC IN MAIN."
!   023614.00  "-SUBJ IN MAIN."
!   023624.00  "-INT ON EXIC TO PSIC ON MAIN TO"          <- DECK TYPO
!   023624.40  "-VFL LOAD IN MAIN."
!   023625.40  "-EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT"
!   023626.00  "-FOLLOWING PSEUDO IC."
!   023627.00  "-EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT"
!   023627.40  "-FOLLOWING INSTRUCT ADDRESSED BY PSIC."
!   023631.40  "-EXIC SUBJ INST NOT EXECUTED."
!   023634.00  "-BITS 0-24 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD."
!   023636.40  "-BITS 28-45 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD."
!   023641.00  "-BITS 46-63 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD."
!   023643.00  "-INST AT PSIC WAS EXECUTED."
!   023645.00  "-PSEUDO IC UNCHANGED BY EXIC."
!   023645.40  "-EXIC IN MAIN."
!   023646.00  "-PSIC IN IX STG."
!   023646.40  "-SUBJ IN MAIN."
!   023657.40  "-INT ON EXIC TO PSIC IN IX STG"
!   023660.00  "-TO VFL LOAD IN MAIN."
!   023661.00  "-EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT"
!   023661.40  "-FOLLOWING PSEUDO IC."
!   023662.40  "-EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT"
!   023663.00  "-FOLLOWING INSTRUCT ADDRESSED BY PSIC."
!   023665.00  "-EXIC SUBJ INST NOT EXECUTED."
!   023667.40  "-BITS 0-24 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD."
!   023672.00  "-BITS 28-45 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD."
!   023674.40  "-BITS 46-63 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD."
!   023676.40  "-INST AT PSIC WAS EXECUTED."
!   023700.40  "-PSEUDO IC UNCHANGED BY EXIC."
!   023702.40  "-TO SSIP."
!   023703.40  "-UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK."
!
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! DECK TYPO vs SCAN DAMAGE -- ONE TYPO, TWO NON-EVENTS, ZERO DAMAGE
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! 1. 023624.00 "-INT ON EXIC TO PSIC ON MAIN TO" -- DECK TYPO, and the
!    control is the SAME WORD ON A PARALLEL LINE.  023606.40 prints the
!    identical message with "IN MAIN".  Measured at 500 dpi by
!    segmenting glyph bounding boxes from pixel-column ink profiles:
!      023606.40, the glyph before "N MAIN":  11 px bare stroke = I.
!                 letter O on the SAME row ("ON EXIC", "TO", "TO"):
!                 44, 44, 44 px.
!      023624.00, the glyph in the SAME word position:  44 px round.
!                 letter O on the SAME row ("ON EXIC" 42, "TO" 45).
!    44 against 44/42/45 on its own line and against 11 on the parallel
!    line.  It is a CLEAN, fully-formed, correctly-inked letter O in a
!    place where the word is "IN" -- a clean wrong letter, which is a
!    typo.  Damage would have left a RAGGED I; nothing here is ragged,
!    and no other glyph on that row or its neighbours is degraded.
!    TRANSCRIBED AS PRINTED.
!
! 2. 023577.00 "-RELINQUISH CONTROL,AND THE TWO" has NO SPACE after the
!    comma.  Settled by PITCH, not by eye, because a missing space and a
!    dropped character look alike.  Cell pitch measured on the same row
!    from the well-formed word "CONTROL": starts at 2605, 2654, 2704,
!    2755, 2807, 2854, 2905 px -- 49, 50, 51, 52, 47, 51, mean 50.0 px
!    per cell.  A word gap on the same row measures 101 px (H of
!    RELINQUISH at 2504 -> C of CONTROL at 2605), 100 px (D of AND 3108
!    -> T of THE 3208) and 99 px (E of THE 3309 -> T of TWO 3408), i.e.
!    exactly TWO cells.  The comma's cell begins at 2955 (L at 2905 plus
!    one 50 px cell) and the A of AND begins at 3006 -- 51 px, ONE cell.
!    So the comma and the A are adjacent cells: no space was dropped by
!    the scan, the deck printed none.  AN AUTHORING QUIRK, NOT A GARBLE;
!    not forced into the typo/damage binary.
!
! 3. 023657.40 "-INT ON EXIC TO PSIC IN IX STG" ends without a period
!    and its sentence's "TO" is carried to the next line
!    ("-TO VFL LOAD IN MAIN.").  Checked on the ink profile: after the
!    G at x 3443 (w 40) there is no ink at all before the machine-code
!    column at x 4202.  That is NOT a dropped period -- the parallel row
!    023606.40 likewise ends "IN MAIN TO" with no period, because in
!    both cases the sentence continues on the next line.  Non-event.
!
! 4. "INSTRUCT" for "instruction" and "CHNGD." for "changed" are the
!    deck's own abbreviations, printed identically four times and four
!    times respectively.  Not drops.
!
! NOTHING IN 137 ROWS IS SCAN-DAMAGED.  Every character on pp.96-98 is
! a clean, well-inked print; no letter is ragged and no stroke is
! broken.  Said plainly rather than manufactured into a finding.
!
! THE LABEL GLYPH, RE-MEASURED ON THIS BLOCK'S OWN PAGE rather than
! inherited from docs/listing_typography.md.  Row 023576.40 at 500 dpi:
!   name field "I6247":   I 10 px | 6 39 | 2 36 | 4 42 | 7 ...
!   operand "LVI,$X1,I62INT" on the SAME ROW:
!     L 37 | V 30 | I 10 | , 25 | $ 36 | X 38 | 1 31 | , 23 |
!     I 11 | 6 37 | 2 34 | I 12 | N 38 | T ...
! Three letter-I glyphs (10, 11, 12 px) and one digit 1 (31 px) on one
! printed row.  The populations do not touch.  The labels are I6247,
! I6248, ..., I6259 and the externals are I62INT, I62PSI, IC262.
!
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! A FULL-WORD INSTRUCTION AT AN ODD HALF-WORD, TWICE, AND NO CNOP
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! 023641.40 "L(BU),$X0" and 023663.40 "L(BU),$R" each START on a .40 and
! STRADDLE into the next word: the listing's own next printed addresses
! are 023642.40 and 023664.40, two half-words on.  The other two
! full-word rows (023630.00, 023675.00) are word-aligned.  THE LISTING
! PRINTS NO CNOP ANYWHERE IN THE BLOCK and the printed address column
! proves there is no gap, so none is written here.
! CHECKED, not assumed: assembling "SLC,(8)23641.00 / B,SERS /
! L(BU),$X0 / SIC,SEN / BD,SERS" puts the VFL load's two halves at
! 023641.40 and 023642.00 and the SIC at 023642.40, matching the page.
! AND IT IS NOT A REPO FIRST: a sweep of every ROWS tuple in every
! verify_*.py here finds 656 full-word rows, 216 of them at a .40.
!
! ------------------------------------------------------------------
! ENCODING ONLY, and it could not be otherwise.  Every one of the six
! checks needs machinery this model does not have: the 64-word
! interrupt table I62INT, 1260's clear-indicators subroutine I60S1, the
! subject constants on PDF p.109, and EXIC itself, which this model
! does not EXECUTE.  EXIC is in MISC_CODES, so the ASSEMBLER encodes
! it; that is the whole distinction.
!
! Transcription standard: bit-exact against the printed machine code,
! verify_ax5b_162_test2a_listing.py.

        SLC, (8)23576.40

! ==================================================================
! PASS 0 -- PDF p.96.  The bare relinquish test.  No verification body.
! ==================================================================
I6247  LVI, $X1, I62INT           ! -TEST 2A, CHECK THAT EXIC WILL NOT
        SVA, $X1, $IA             ! -RELINQUISH CONTROL,AND THE TWO
        LVI, $X1, I6248           ! -POSSIBLE MEMORY COMBINATIONS.
        SVA, $X1, I62ITE          ! plant the no-interrupt error entry
        SIC, I60SX1
        B,   I60S1                 ! 1260's clear-indicators subroutine
        LVI, $X1, I62SUB
        SVA, $X1, I62PSI          ! aim the pseudo-IC at the subject slot
        LVI, $X1, I6249
        SVA, $X1, I62BR1          ! trap 1: the half-word AFTER the PSIC
        LVI, $X1, I6250
        SVA, $X1, I62BR2          ! trap 2: the half-word AFTER the SUBJ
        LX,  $X1, I62EXV          ! the subject: full-word "L(BU),I00O"
        SX,  $X1, I62SUB
        EXIC, I62PSI
        BD,  I6251                 ! -PSIC IS PSEUDO IC.
!
! ---- pass 0, the interruption trap -------------------------------
I6248  SIC, SEN                   ! -INT ON EXIC TO PSIC IN MAIN TO
        BD,  SERS                  ! -VFL LOAD IN MAIN.
        BD,  I6251
!
! ---- pass 0, trap 1: control after the pseudo-IC ------------------
I6249  SIC, SEN                   ! -EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT
        BD,  SERS                  ! -FOLLOWING PSEUDO IC.
        BD,  I6251
!
! ---- pass 0, trap 2: control after the subject --------------------
!   No "BD,I6251" here: this entry falls straight through into I6251.
I6250  SIC, SEN                   ! -EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT
        BD,  SERS                  ! -FOLLOWING INSTRUCT ADDRESSED BY PSIC.

! ==================================================================
! PASS 1 -- PDF pp.96-97.  Same memory configuration, full body.
! ==================================================================
I6251  LVI, $X1, I6252            ! -TEST MEMORY COMBOS.
        SVA, $X1, I62ITE          ! -EXIC IN MAIN.
        LVI, $X1, I62SUB          ! -PSIC IN MAIN.
        SVA, $X1, I62PSI          ! -SUBJ IN MAIN.
        Z,   $X0                   ! check 5's witness: PSIC not executed
        LVI, $X1, I6253
        SVA, $X1, I62BR1
        LX,  $X1, I62EXV
        SX,  $X1, I62SUB
        LVI, $X1, I6254
        SVA, $X1, I62BR2
        SIC, I60SX1
        BD,  I60S1                 ! BD here; pass 2 uses B.  Not a typo.
        Z,   $IND
        Z,   $MASK
        Z,   $R                    ! check 1's witness: subject executed
        Z,   $L
        EXIC, I62PSI
        BD,  I6255
!
! ---- pass 1, the interruption trap --------------------------------
I6252  SIC, SEN                   ! -INT ON EXIC TO PSIC ON MAIN TO
        BD,  SERS                  ! -VFL LOAD IN MAIN.
        BD,  I6255
!
! ---- pass 1, trap 1 -----------------------------------------------
I6253  SIC, SEN                   ! -EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT
        BD,  SERS                  ! -FOLLOWING PSEUDO IC.
        BD,  I6255
!
! ---- pass 1, trap 2 (PDF p.97 begins) -----------------------------
I6254  SIC, SEN                   ! -EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT
        BD,  SERS                  ! -FOLLOWING INSTRUCT ADDRESSED BY PSIC.
!
! ---- pass 1, the verification body --------------------------------
I6255  L(BU), $R                  ! FULL WORD, word-aligned here
        SIC, SEN
        BRZ, SERS                  ! -EXIC SUBJ INST NOT EXECUTED.
!
        LX,  $X14, I62EXV          ! the master subject
        LX,  $X15, I62SUB          ! the working copy
        KV,  $X14, $X15            ! VALUE fields, bits 0-24
        SIC, SEN
        BZXE, SERS                 ! -BITS 0-24 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD.
!
        SC,  $X15, $X15            ! COUNT -> VALUE so KV can see it
        SC,  $X14, $X14            ! X15 FIRST here; pass 2 reverses it
        KV,  $X14, $X15
        SIC, SEN
        BZXE, SERS                 ! -BITS 28-45 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD.
!
        SR,  $X15, $X15            ! REFILL -> VALUE
        SR,  $X14, $X14            ! X15 FIRST here; pass 2 reverses it
        KV,  $X14, $X15
        SIC, SEN
        BZXE, SERS                 ! -BITS 46-63 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD.
!
        L(BU), $X0                 ! FULL WORD STRADDLING 023641.40/642.00
        SIC, SEN
        BZRZ, SERS                 ! -INST AT PSIC WAS EXECUTED.
!
        LX,  $X1, I62PSI           ! the pseudo-IC word itself
        KVI, $X1, I62SUB           ! still where it started?
        SIC, SEN
        BXE, SERS                  ! -PSEUDO IC UNCHANGED BY EXIC.

! ==================================================================
! PASS 2 -- PDF pp.97-98.  PSIC in index storage.
! ==================================================================
!   No "-TEST MEMORY COMBOS." heading: the three class comments start
!   one row higher than pass 1's.
        LVI, $X1, I6256           ! -EXIC IN MAIN.
        SVA, $X1, I62ITE          ! -PSIC IN IX STG.
        LVI, $X1, I62SUB          ! -SUBJ IN MAIN.
        SVA, $X1, I62PSI
        Z,   $X0
        LVI, $X1, I6257
        SVA, $X1, I62BR1
        LX,  $X1, I62EXV
        SX,  $X1, I62SUB
        LVI, $X1, I6258
        SVA, $X1, I62BR2
        SIC, I60SX1
        B,   I60S1                 ! B here; pass 1 uses BD.  Not a typo.
        LX,  $X2, I62PSI           ! THE COMBINATION: PSIC into index 2
        Z,   $IND
        Z,   $MASK
        Z,   $R
        Z,   $L
        EXIC, $X2                  ! ...and the EXIC points at index 2
        BD,  I6259
!
! ---- pass 2, the interruption trap --------------------------------
I6256  SIC, SEN                   ! -INT ON EXIC TO PSIC IN IX STG
        BD,  SERS                  ! -TO VFL LOAD IN MAIN.
        BD,  I6259
!
! ---- pass 2, trap 1 (PDF p.98 begins) -----------------------------
I6257  SIC, SEN                   ! -EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT
        BD,  SERS                  ! -FOLLOWING PSEUDO IC.
        BD,  I6259
!
! ---- pass 2, trap 2 -----------------------------------------------
I6258  SIC, SEN                   ! -EXIC RELINQUISHES CONTROL TO INSTRUCT
        BD,  SERS                  ! -FOLLOWING INSTRUCT ADDRESSED BY PSIC.
!
! ---- pass 2, the verification body --------------------------------
I6259  L(BU), $R                  ! FULL WORD STRADDLING 023663.40/664.00
        SIC, SEN
        BRZ, SERS                  ! -EXIC SUBJ INST NOT EXECUTED.
!
        LX,  $X14, I62EXV
        LX,  $X15, I62SUB
        KV,  $X14, $X15
        SIC, SEN
        BZXE, SERS                 ! -BITS 0-24 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD.
!
        SC,  $X14, $X14            ! X14 FIRST here -- pass 1 has X15
        SC,  $X15, $X15
        KV,  $X14, $X15
        SIC, SEN
        BZXE, SERS                 ! -BITS 28-45 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD.
!
        SR,  $X14, $X14            ! X14 FIRST here -- pass 1 has X15
        SR,  $X15, $X15
        KV,  $X14, $X15
        SIC, SEN
        BZXE, SERS                 ! -BITS 46-63 OF SUBJ INST CHNGD.
!
        L(BU), $X0                 ! FULL WORD, word-aligned here
        SIC, SEN
        BZRZ, SERS                 ! -INST AT PSIC WAS EXECUTED.
!
        LX,  $X1, $X2              ! the pseudo-IC IN INDEX STORAGE
        KVI, $X1, I62SUB
        SIC, SEN
        BXE, SERS                  ! -PSEUDO IC UNCHANGED BY EXIC.
!
! ---- routine 1262's TEST 2A exit ---------------------------------
        B,   $+1.0                 ! computed target 023702.00; bit 18 = 0
        BD,  I6247                 ! the restart link: TEST 2A's own entry
        SIC, SEN0+.32
        B,   SSW                   ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  $+.32                 ! computed target 023703.40; BIT 18 = 1
!
! ---- the continuity bridge ---------------------------------------
        LX,  $X13, IC262          ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
        V+,  $X13, BIT4           ! TEST 2A done = bit 4
        SX,  $X13, IC262

! ---- externals, SYN'd at the addresses this same deck prints -----
!   THESE ARE INPUTS TO THE CHECK, NOT WITNESSES.  No label row
!   defining any of them appears on PDF pp.96/97/98; every address below
!   comes from an OPERAND field or from another page of the same deck.
!   See the verify script's docstring for the tiering.
SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0             ! the SIC error-entry link
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0             ! the error-report routine
SEN0    SYN, (8)1311.0             ! the DIGIT zero -- see the verify file
SSW     SYN, (8)1301.0             ! -TO SSIP.
I60S1  SYN, (8)22741.0            ! 1260's clear-indicators subroutine
I60SX1 SYN, (8)23041.0            ! its SIC return link
I62INT SYN, (8)24220.0            ! the 64-word interrupt table
I62ITE SYN, (8)24320.0            ! the interrupt-table entry 1262 plants
I62PSI SYN, (8)24323.0            ! the pseudo-IC word, "LX,$X0,0"
I62BR1 SYN, (8)24323.40           ! trap 1, the RIGHT half of I62PSI's word
I62SUB SYN, (8)24324.0            ! the subject-instruction slot
I62BR2 SYN, (8)24325.0            ! trap 2, after the FULL-WORD subject
I62EXV SYN, (8)24327.0            ! the subject, "L(BU),I00O"
IC262  SYN, (8)24171.0            ! 1262's continuity register
BIT4   SYN, (8)24526.0            ! the BIT table's bit 4 word
        END, I6247
